    solution_overview: "A workshop owns the tool set $W = \\{\\text{hammer}, \\text{saw}, \\text{level}, \\text{pliers}\\}$. The mobile kit is $K = \\{\\text{hammer}, \\text{pliers}\\}$, and the measuring kit is $M = \\{\\text{level}\\}$.\n\n**Part 1: Setup.**\n\nThe full workshop set has four tools. The mobile kit contains only the hammer and pliers, while the measuring kit contains only the level.\n\n**Part 2: Key facts.**\n\n$A\\subsetneq B$ means $A\\subseteq B$ and $A\\ne B$. A set is always a subset of itself, but never a proper subset of itself.\n\n**Part 3: Solve.**\n\n**1.** (TRUE) $K \\subsetneq W$.\n\nEach item in $K$ is in $W$, and $W$ also has a saw and a level. Thus $K$ is a proper subset.\n\n**2.** (FALSE) $W \\subsetneq W$.\n\nEvery set is a subset of itself, but a proper subset must be strictly smaller. Therefore $W\\not\\subsetneq W$.\n\n**3.** (FALSE) $M \\subseteq K$.\n\nThe level belongs to $W$ but is not in the mobile kit $K$.\n\n**4.** (FALSE) $\\{\\text{hammer},\\text{saw}\\} \\subseteq K$.\n\nAlthough the hammer is in $K$, the saw is not. One missing element prevents this subset claim.\n\n**5.** (TRUE) $K \\subseteq W$.\n\nBoth hammer and pliers are tools in $W$, so all elements of $K$ are contained in $W$.\n\n**Answer.** A=TRUE, B=FALSE, C=FALSE, D=FALSE, E=TRUE",
