    sort_order: 11,
    solution_overview: "An event offers badge colours in the set $C = \\{\\text{blue}, \\text{gold}, \\text{silver}, \\text{violet}\\}$. A colour selection is any subset of $C$.\n\n**Part 1: Setup.**\n\nThere are four available colours. Every subset of $C$ is one possible selection, including $\\emptyset$ and $C$ itself.\n\n**Part 2: Key facts.**\n\nFor a finite set with $n$ elements, $|\\mathcal{P}(C)|=2^n$. The number of $k$-element subsets is $\\binom{n}{k}$.\n\n**Part 3: Solve.**\n\n**1.** (TRUE) $|\\mathcal{P}(C)| = 16$.\n\nSince $|C|=4$, its power set has $2^4=16$ subsets.\n\n**2.** (FALSE) $\\mathcal{P}(C)$ has 4 elements.\n\nThe four colours are elements of $C$, but $\\mathcal{P}(C)$ contains all 16 possible selections.\n\n**3.** (TRUE) $\\{\\text{blue},\\text{gold}\\} \\in \\mathcal{P}(C)$.\n\nBoth blue and gold belong to $C$, so their set is a subset of $C$ and therefore an element of $\\mathcal{P}(C)$.\n\n**4.** (FALSE) $\\{\\text{blue},\\text{teal}\\} \\in \\mathcal{P}(C)$.\n\nTeal is not one of the available colours, so this set is not a subset of $C$.\n\n**5.** (TRUE) There are 6 selections containing exactly two colours.\n\nA two-colour selection is formed by choosing 2 of the 4 colours: $\\binom{4}{2}=6$.\n\n**Answer.** A=TRUE, B=FALSE, C=TRUE, D=FALSE, E=TRUE",
