      "**B) $-7 \\notin R$.**  (false)\n\nBecause $(-7)^2=49$, the integer $-7$ belongs to $R$.\n\nThe claim is **false**.",
      "**C) $P \\subsetneq R$.**  (true)\n\nThe only element of $P$ is 7, which is in $R$; $R$ has the additional element $-7$, so the inclusion is proper.\n\nThe claim is **true**.",
