    solution_overview: "Let $U=\\{a,b,c,d\\}$. A partition of $U$ is a collection of nonempty pairwise disjoint subsets whose union is $U$.\n\n**Part 1: Setup.**\n\nA candidate partition must pass three checks: every block is nonempty, distinct blocks do not overlap, and the blocks cover all of $U$.\n\n**Part 2: Key facts.**\n\nA partition can have one block, several blocks, or one block for each element. Its number of blocks need not equal the number of elements.\n\n**Part 3: Solve.**\n\n**1.** (TRUE) $\\big\\{\\{a,b\\},\\{c,d\\}\\big\\}$ is a partition of $U$.\n\nThe two blocks are nonempty, share no elements, and together contain $a,b,c,d$.\n\n**2.** (FALSE) $\\big\\{\\{a,b\\},\\{b,c\\},\\{d\\}\\big\\}$ is a partition of $U$.\n\nThe element $b$ occurs in both of the first two blocks, so the blocks are not pairwise disjoint.\n\n**3.** (TRUE) $\\big\\{\\{a\\},\\{b\\},\\{c\\},\\{d\\}\\big\\}$ is a partition of $U$.\n\nEach singleton block is nonempty, no two share an element, and all four elements are covered.\n\n**4.** (FALSE) $\\big\\{\\{a,b,c\\}\\big\\}$ is a partition of $U$.\n\nThis collection misses $d$, so its union is not all of $U$.\n\n**5.** (TRUE) $\\big\\{U\\big\\}$ is a partition of $U$.\n\nThe single nonempty block $U$ covers every element and has no second block with which it could overlap.\n\n**Answer.** A=TRUE, B=FALSE, C=TRUE, D=FALSE, E=TRUE",
