    solution_overview: "|$Reps \\times Accounts$| = |Reps|·|Accounts| = 5·8 = 40, and this scales directly with team size (6·8=48). Ordered-pair convention: (rep,account) $Reps \\times Accounts$ requires the FIRST coordinate from Reps and $second \\in from$ Accounts - reversing the order breaks the definition, and if either set\n\n**Part 1: Setup.**\n\n|$Reps \\times Accounts$| = |Reps|·|Accounts| = 5·8 = 40, and this scales directly with team size (6·8=48). Ordered-pair convention: (rep,account) $Reps \\times Accounts$ requires the FIRST coordinate from Reps and $second \\in from$ Accounts - reversing the order breaks the definition, and if either set is empty, the whole product is empty.\n\n**Part 2: Key facts.**\n\nUse the definitions of membership, subset, union, intersection, difference, complement, and power set as needed. Compute shared objects once.\n\n**Part 3: Solve.**\n\n**1.** (TRUE) The total number of possible (rep, account) pairs is 40.\n\nEach of the 5 reps can be paired with each of the 8 accounts, giving $5 \\times 8$ = 40 possible ordered pairs - this is exactly the size of the Cartesian product $Reps \\times Accounts$.\n\n**2.** (FALSE) The pair (Maria, Account 3) is the same coverage assignment as (Account 3, Maria).\n\nOrdered pairs respect order and the identity of each coordinate set: (Maria, Account 3) belongs to $Reps \\times Accounts$, while (Account 3, Maria) would belong to $Accounts \\times Reps$ - a different set. They are not the same object.\n\n**3.** (TRUE) If the firm currently has zero client accounts, no coverage assignments can be formed no matter how many reps it hires.\n\nIf Accounts = , then $Reps \\times Accounts$ = regardless of how many reps exist, since there is $no \\emptyset \\emptyset$ account to pair with any rep. This mirrors the general fact that $A \\times$= for any set A.$\\emptyset \\emptyset$\n\n**4.** (FALSE) $In the pair (rep, account), the statement \"(Maria, Account 3) belongs to Reps \\times Accounts\" means Maria \\in Accounts and Account 3 Reps. \\in$\n\nBy the definition of the Cartesian product, (Maria, Account 3) $Reps \\times Accounts$ means $Maria \\in \\in$ Reps and Account 3 Accounts - the statement has the membership reversed.$\\in$\n\n**5.** (TRUE) If the firm hires one more rep (6 reps total) while keeping 8 accounts, the number of possible assignments becomes 48.\n\n$With 6 reps and 8 accounts, the number of ordered pairs is 6 \\times 8 = 48, confirming the statement exactly.$\n\n**Answer.** A=TRUE, B=FALSE, C=TRUE, D=FALSE, E=TRUE",
