      "**A) √2 + (-√2) = 0 is a valid counterexample to \"the sum of two irrational numbers is always irrational,\" since √2 and -√2 are irrational but their sum, 0, is rational**  (true)\n\n√2 and -√2 are both irrational, yet their sum is 0, which is rational - exactly one counterexample is needed to break the universal claim.\n\nThe claim matches the computation above, so it is **true**.",
