      "**D) $To prove a universal statement \" x, P(x)\" is true, it suffices to check it for x = 1 and x = 2 \\forall$**  (false)\n\nTrap: checking a finite number of cases, however many, never proves a universal statement about infinitely many (or even just many) values - a single untested case could still be a counterexample.\n\nThis is a common trap; the corrected reading shows the claim is **false**.",
