      "**A) \"This dolphin lives in water, so it must be a fish\" uses the converse of the rule and is an invalid argument.**  (true)\n\nThe argument has form Q P, the converse of P Q. It's invalid, and dolphins prove it: they live $in \\Rightarrow \\Rightarrow$ water yet are mammals, not fish.\n\nThe claim matches the computation above, so it is **true**.",
