      "**D) The correct negation of the overall statement is: “There exists a positive integer m such that for every positive integer n, m·n ≠ 100.”**  (true)\n\nNegating “for every m, there exists n such that mn=100” correctly flips the quantifiers ( →, →)$\\forall \\exists$\\exists \\forall$ and negates the equation, giving exactly this.\n\nThe claim matches the computation above, so it is **true**.",
