    solution_overview: "Test the only two possibilities for X directly. If X is a liar, X's claim (\"Y lies\") is false, so Y is a truth-teller - but then Y's own claim would have to be true, forcing Y to be a liar too, a contradiction. So X must be a truth-teller; then Y is a liar, and everything Y says\n\n**Part 1: Setup.**\n\nTest the only two possibilities for X directly. If X is a liar, X's claim (\"Y lies\") is false, so Y is a truth-teller - but then Y's own claim would have to be true, forcing Y to be a liar too, a contradiction. So X must be a truth-teller; then Y is a liar, and everything Y says (including this statement) is false - consistent. This is the unique solution.\n\n**Part 2: Key facts.**\n\nNegation switches quantifiers: $\\neg \\forall x\\, P(x) \\equiv \\exists x\\, \\neg P(x)$ and $\\neg \\exists x\\, P(x) \\equiv \\forall x\\, \\neg P(x)$. For deduction puzzles, exhaust consistent assignments.\n\n**Part 3: Solve.**\n\n**1.** (TRUE) X is a truth-teller.\n\nSuppose X is a liar: then X's claim “Y always lies” is false, so Y is a truth-teller; but then Y's statement “X and I are both liars” must be true, meaning Y is a liar - contradicting that Y is a truth-teller. So X cannot be a liar; X must be a truth-teller.\n\n**2.** (FALSE) Y is a truth-teller.\n\nSince X is a truth-teller (part a), X's statement “Y always lies” is true, so Y is a liar.\n\n**3.** (TRUE) Y's statement (“X and I are both liars”) is false.\n\nSince Y is a liar (part b), everything Y says is false, including this statement.\n\n**4.** (FALSE) There are two equally valid solutions for the types of X and Y.\n\nOnly one consistent assignment exists (X truth-teller, Y liar); the alternative (X liar) leads to a direct contradiction, as shown in (a), so it is not a valid solution.\n\n**5.** (TRUE) If X were a liar, this would lead to a logical contradiction.\n\nThis is exactly the contradiction demonstrated in part (a): assuming X is a liar forces Y to be simultaneously a truth-teller and a liar.\n\n**Answer.** A=TRUE, B=FALSE, C=TRUE, D=FALSE, E=TRUE",
